WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.667 --> 00:00:15.942
Summer passed quickly.

2
00:00:15.943 --> 00:00:20.167
The leaves started to fall from the trees.

3
00:00:20.168 --> 00:00:24.697
Thumbelina was tired and her clothes were torn.

4
00:00:24.698 --> 00:00:28.522
Thumbelina noticed some nuts on the ground.

5
00:00:28.523 --> 00:00:31.306
She picked up a small one.

6
00:00:31.307 --> 00:00:35.869
"Hey, that's mine!" yelled a squirrel.

7
00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:40.390
"I found it first," she said stubbornly.

8
00:00:40.391 --> 00:00:46.915
"Okay, I guess you're getting ready for the winter too," replied the squirrel.

9
00:00:46.916 --> 00:00:51.350
"Winter?" said Thumbelina. "What's that?"

10
00:00:51.351 --> 00:00:56.021
Surprised, the squirrel shook her tail.

11
00:00:56.022 --> 00:01:01.889
"Winter is when it gets cold, silly," said the squirrel.

12
00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:04.974
"Food is hard to find.

13
00:01:04.975 --> 00:01:08.975
You have to gather and store food.

14
00:01:08.976 --> 00:01:11.877
That's what I'm doing."

15
00:01:11.878 --> 00:01:17.751
The squirrel grabbed another nut and quickly ran up a tree.

16
00:01:17.752 --> 00:01:20.805
The days did get colder.

17
00:01:20.806 --> 00:01:26.007
And food was hard to find.

18
00:01:26.008 --> 00:01:32.302
One day, hungry and tired, Thumbelina fell asleep.

19
00:01:32.303 --> 00:01:37.144
She had a dream she was in a warm bed.

20
00:01:37.145 --> 00:01:46.324
Beautiful voices were singing.

21
00:01:46.325 --> 00:01:48.168
Thumbelina woke up.

22
00:01:48.169 --> 00:01:50.943
She wasn't dreaming.

23
00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:56.460
"Where am I?" she asked, rubbing her eyes.

24
00:01:56.461 --> 00:01:59.374
"You're safe, dear," said a bird.

25
00:01:59.375 --> 00:02:02.136
Thumbelina sat up.

26
00:02:02.137 --> 00:02:06.031
She was inside a bird's nest.

27
00:02:06.032 --> 00:02:08.284
"We thought you needed help.

28
00:02:08.285 --> 00:02:12.038
So we brought you to our house," said the bird.

29
00:02:12.039 --> 00:02:15.041
"I'm Maggie."

30
00:02:15.042 --> 00:02:17.488
"I heard something lovely,"

31
00:02:17.489 --> 00:02:21.615
Thumbelina said after introducing herself.

32
00:02:21.616 --> 00:02:24.960
"We were singing," said the other bird.

33
00:02:24.961 --> 00:02:27.126
"My name is Kris."

34
00:02:27.127 --> 00:02:32.311
"I haven't sung in a long time," said Thumbelina.

35
00:02:32.312 --> 00:02:37.573
"I used to sing when I was happy."

36
00:02:37.574 --> 00:02:42.916
"Well, not all songs are happy ones," said Maggie.

37
00:02:42.917 --> 00:02:46.838
"What do you mean?" asked Thumbelina.

38
00:02:46.839 --> 00:02:50.349
Kris and Maggie looked at each other.

39
00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:54.021
"All songs are different," said Kris.

40
00:02:54.022 --> 00:03:00.612
"Listen to this one."

41
00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:07.024
His song was short and almost angry.

42
00:03:07.025 --> 00:03:11.332
"You sounded upset," said Thumbelina.

43
00:03:11.333 --> 00:03:15.542
Kris nodded. "That was an angry song."

44
00:03:15.543 --> 00:03:27.936
"Can you guess this one?" asked Maggie.

45
00:03:27.937 --> 00:03:38.052
Her song was slow and quiet.

46
00:03:38.053 --> 00:03:41.441
"No, I can't," said Thumbelina.

47
00:03:41.442 --> 00:03:44.000
"What kind of song is that?"

48
00:03:44.001 --> 00:03:49.809
"I sing that song when I need to solve a problem," said Maggie.

49
00:03:49.810 --> 00:03:54.589
"Can you teach me some songs?" asked Thumbelina.

50
00:03:54.590 --> 00:03:58.722
"Of course," said Maggie.

51
00:03:58.723 --> 00:04:03.586
They taught Thumbelina many kinds of bird songs.

52
00:04:03.587 --> 00:04:06.630
Each song was special.

53
00:04:06.631 --> 00:04:12.766
But one kind of song was a secret language.

54
00:04:12.767 --> 00:04:21.640
These songs were talking songs, and Thumbelina learned these too.

55
00:04:21.641 --> 00:04:26.666
Thumbelina stayed with her friends Kris and Maggie.

56
00:04:26.667 --> 00:04:32.670
The birds brought her food and kept her warm.

57
00:04:32.671 --> 00:04:37.163
But soon the birds had to leave.

58
00:04:37.164 --> 00:04:40.922
"Winter is almost here," said Maggie.

59
00:04:40.923 --> 00:04:44.284
"It's time for us to fly south."

60
00:04:44.285 --> 00:04:49.391
"I wish I had wings," Thumbelina said sadly.

61
00:04:49.392 --> 00:04:52.887
"Then I could fly away with you."

62
00:04:52.888 --> 00:04:59.771
The birds put her on the ground and sang a song of good-bye.

63
00:04:59.772 --> 00:05:05.452
"Good-bye, Thumbelina," they said.

64
00:05:05.453 --> 00:05:11.007
"You'll find your way home!"

65
00:05:11.008 --> 00:05:20.108
"Good-bye, my friends," she replied.

66
00:05:20.109 --> 00:05:28.778
Kris and Maggie flew off.
